# trace10.err -- Next actions item 8: the one traced LaserTank.lvl level-10 run, session 29.
#
# Why it is here and not in build/reports/: it is the whole output of a 26m53s run at --jobs 1,
# it is the evidence behind SOLVER.md's diagnosis of level 10, and it is not cheap to reproduce.
# Nothing parses it but a human.  See bench/README.md for the rule that admits an output here.
#
# The command as run, with one difference: the run redirected to build/trace10.err and the file
# was moved here afterwards, so a re-run should write straight to bench/ as shown.
#
#   build/lasertank-solve.exe --levels data/levels/LaserTank.lvl --level 10 \
#     --no-ida --no-beam --push --push-read --push-eval work --read-antitank-wall \
#     --push-reach --push-ferry-match --push-ferry-maze \
#     --push-dead 20 --push-fire 8 --push-shot-run 16 \
#     --push-beam 1024 --push-restarts 0 --max-keys 5000 \
#     --push-trace --nodes 400000000 --budget-ms 14400000 --jobs 1 \
#     --out build/trace10 2> bench/trace10.err
#
# Result: unsolved, stopped on `budget` at d=63 / 399,019,729 nodes / 26m53s (247k nodes/s,
# ~6.2M a depth).  What the columns say, and it is all five in the one run:
#
#   trunc=    0 at every one of the 64 depths     -- the closure never truncates
#   front=    1024 at every depth past d=1        -- the frontier never dies
#   boards=   1024 of 1024                        -- no duplicate poses at this width
#   barrier   0 of 63,454 expansions              -- THE finding: the read names nothing
#   best=     62 -> 22 by d=18, then 28 from d=36 to d=63 (28 depths, worse than halfway)
#
# It also reached d=63, past the 53 board changes of the level's own hand line, so depth was
# never the constraint.  Level 10 is a GAUNTLET (`--analyze`: "what is in the way is fire, not
# terrain", on the barrier: 0), so the barrier set is empty by construction and layers 6-8 are
# inert on it.  For contrast the same instrument reads 74.7% of expansions with a barrier on
# ferry-levels.txt and 72.1% on deep-levels.txt.
#
# SOLVER.md: Next actions item 8, and the level-10 bullet of What has not fallen.
#
